From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:49:19 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: b43: let mac80211 handle the keys of ciphers b43 can't
 offload

b43_op_set_key() returns -EINVAL, after a B43_WARN_ON(), for every
cipher other than WEP, TKIP and CCMP. mac80211 still falls back to
software crypto for CCMP-256, GCMP, GCMP-256 and the BIP ciphers, but
logs "failed to set key ... to hardware (-22)" for each such key.

Return -EOPNOTSUPP, which tells mac80211 the cipher is not offloaded,
and drop the warning: these keys are expected.

Tested with WPA2 GCMP-256, PMF with BIP-GMAC-256, SAE and CCMP: the
links pass traffic and nothing is logged.

Fixes: e4d6b7951812 ("[B43]: add mac80211-based driver for modern BCM43xx devices")
Signed-off-by: Rosen Penev <rosenp@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/b43/main.c
@@ -4254,7 +4254,8 @@ static int b43_op_set_key(struct ieee802
 		algorithm = B43_SEC_ALGO_AES;
 		break;
 	default:
-		B43_WARN_ON(1);
+		/* CCMP-256, GCMP and BIP keys are handled by mac80211 */
+		err = -EOPNOTSUPP;
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
 	index = (u8) (key->keyidx);
